{"question_id": "V2-dev-LAW-en-T3-002", "approach": "LEX5B", "approach_base": "LEX5B", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "L", "corpus_set": "LAW_en", "answer_text": "Bribery Act 2010, failure to prevent bribery - enforcement/punishment: NOT_FOUND\nModern Slavery Act 2015, s.54 duties - enforcement: \"The duties imposed on commercial organisations by this section are enforceable by the Secretary of State bringing civil proceedings in the High Court for an injunction or, in Scotland, for specific performance of a statutory duty under section 45 of the Court of Session Act 1988.\"\n\nThe Modern Slavery Act 2015 failure to produce a slavery and human trafficking statement is not a criminal offence — it is enforced civilly by the Secretary of State through an injunction (or specific performance in Scotland). The evidence does not state whether the Bribery Act 2010 failure to prevent bribery is a criminal offence or how it is punished, so that part cannot be confirmed.", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 931 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en::o080", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en::p1_b989", "L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en::p1_b990", "L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en::p1_b991", "L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en::p1_b992", "L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en::p1_b993"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [110061, 110992], "meta": {"chunk": 4058, "completed": 58, "prefix": 0, "provenance": [["L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en", 110061, 110992, "body"]]}}, {"text": "[stripped: 1086 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en::o080", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en::p1_b967", "L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en::p1_b968", "L.ukpga-2015-30_modern-slavery-act.en::p1_b969", "L.ukp