{"question_id": "V2-dev-LAW-en-T2-001", "approach": "LEX5B", "approach_base": "LEX5B", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "L", "corpus_set": "LAW_en", "answer_text": "Yes, the Bribery Act 2010 reaches this conduct, as an offence under section 6 (bribery of foreign public officials).\n\n- Section 6 applies because the official of a French ministry is a foreign public official, and the payment is intended to influence the award of a government contract.\n- Under section 12(2), where no act or omission forming part of an offence under section 1, 2 or 6 takes place in the United Kingdom, but the acts or omissions done outside the UK would form part of such an offence if done in the UK, and the person has a close connection with the UK, the acts or omissions form part of the offence and proceedings may be taken at any place in the United Kingdom (section 12(3)).\n- A British citizen has a close connection with the United Kingdom under section 12(4)(a), so the condition in section 12(2)(c) is met.\n- Additionally, section 3(6) confirms that a relevant function or activity counts even if it has no connection with the UK and is performed outside the United Kingdom.", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 853 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::o019", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b167", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b168", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b169", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b170", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b171", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b172", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b173", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b174", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b175", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b176", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b177", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b178", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b179"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "ra